<section class="nhsuk-section" id="cambridge">

    <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-l nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-5">Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust</h2>
    <p class="nhsuk-body">Go live date: 26th November 2025<br> Site: Addenbrooke's</p>
    <p class="nhsuk-body">Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust introduced breast self-referral through NHS 111 online in November 2025, providing eligible patients with a direct digital route into specialist breast diagnostic services.</p>

    <div class="nhsuk-grid-row">
        <ul class="nhsuk-grid-row">
            <li class=" nhsuk-card-group__item">
                <div class="nhsuk-card">
                    <div class="nhsuk-card__content">
                        <p class="nhsuk-body-s" style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-style: italic; color: #005EB8">“Self-referral is a significant step forward in supporting earlier diagnosis and making the most efficient use of our healthcare resources across systems. It is one of the best things we have implemented in recent years. Working with NHS England was fantastic — the whole process was straightforward, and the pathway integrates seamlessly with our existing NHS referral processes. My advice to other hospitals is simple: give it a go!”</p>
                        <p class="nhsuk-body-s" style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">Operations Manager for Cancer <br> Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <h3 class="nhsuk-heading-m nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-2">Engaging their GPs</h3>
    <p class="nhsuk-body">Engagement with local primary care teams formed part of Cambridge's implementation approach, helping to raise awareness of the self-referral pathway and ensure GP practices understood how eligible patients could access breast diagnostic services through NHS 111 online.</p>

